      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverside%2C_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Riverside’s Mission Inn, a Beaux‑Arts courthouse, and the historic Fox Theater together make the downtown skyline a living museum of early 20th‑century architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverside%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Fox Theater famously opened with the first showing of Gone with the Wind in 1939, the most successful film ever.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverside%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Riverside is home to the California Citrus State Historic Park, where the first navel orange tree planted by Eliza Tibbets still stands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverside%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Mount Rubidoux, a city landmark overlooking the Santa Ana River, offers a popular hiking trail that rewards visitors with panoramic views of Riverside.",
